X86 SB
(* The same Store-Buffer shape on x86-TSO. Even the STRONG x86 model ALLOWS
 * this outcome: StoreLoad is the ONE reordering TSO permits. So the bug's
 * window exists on x86 in principle -- it is just almost never observed
 * because the store buffer drains in a few cycles and any locked instruction
 * flushes it. herd7 (Intel's vetted x86tso model) reports this ALLOWED. *)
{ x=0; y=0; }
 P0          | P1          ;
 MOV [x],$1  | MOV [y],$1  ;
 MOV EAX,[y] | MOV EAX,[x] ;
exists
(0:EAX=0 /\ 1:EAX=0)
